This task extracts Fourier Biot-Savart inversion and Hanning regularization. Explicit adaptations: exact odd-length FFT bins replace half-bin-shifted linspace frequencies; centered PSF uses ifftshift rather than fftshift; unobservable K=0 current is fixed to zero before division; full padded two-component field is returned and checked for Hermitian consistency rather than silently discarding an appreciable imaginary field. The original untouched and corrected runs are separately identified in private validation. No unchanged-reproduction claim is made.

Data are original measured flux and independent magnetic-dipole calibration, repackaged into batch-first NPZ. The coarse calibration is the actual upstream zero-pad/cubic-spline preprocessing result, independent of the unknown target. Its small physical-pitch approximation is documented; no normalized or target-fitted kernel is substituted. Current remains in author signed arbitrary units. Paper PDFs and full source are private maintainer evidence, not redistributed here.
